            <ArticleTitle>[Current strategies to minimize of blood loss during radical prostatectomy].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>494-9; quiz 500-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0033-1352497</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prostate cancer is a frequently diagnosed cancer in men with a high incidence. Despite enhancements of surgical techniques in prostatectomyperioperative blood loss is still the most frequent complication. Controlled hypotension (MAP 60-70mmHg) consisting of thoracal epidural anaesthesia und restrictive fluid management is a safe method to minimize blood loss. 25 degrees Trendelenburg position supports the multimodal treatment of controlled hypotension. Tranexamic acid is a safe drug to treat hyperfibrinolysis during prostate resection.</AbstractText>
